{
  "title": "54: al-Qamar القمر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاِقْتَرَبَتِ السَّاعَةُ وَانْشَقَّ الْقَمَرُ‏(1)\nAEQTARABATE SAA-A’TO WAANSHAQQA AL-QAMARU.\nNigh hath come the Hour (of Reckoning) and hath been rent asunder the Moon\nوَاِنْ يَّرَوْا اٰيَةً يُّعْرِضُوْا وَيَقُوْلُوْا سِحْرٌ مُّسْتَمِرٌّ‏(2)\nWA YYARAWA AAYATAL YYUA’REZOOA WAYAQOOLOOA SEHRUM MMUSTAMERRUN.\nAnd if they see a sign, turn they away and say (that it is) sorcery continued\nوَكَذَّبُوْا وَاتَّبَعُوْۤا اَهْوَآءَهُمْ‌ وَكُلُّ اَمْرٍ مُّسْتَقِرٌّ‏(3)\nWA KAZZABOO WAT TABA-O’O AHWAAA-AHUM WA KULLO AMRIN MMUSTAQERRUN.\nAnd they belie (it), and follow they their vain inclinations and every affair is unalterably fixed\nوَلَقَدْ جَآءَهُمْ مِّنَ الْاَنْۢبَآءِ مَا فِيْهِ مُزْدَجَرٌۙ‏(4)\nWA LAQAD JAAA-AHUM MENAL AL-AANBAAE MAA FEEHE MUZDAJARUN.\nAnd indeed, hath come unto them some of the tidings wherein is restraint (from evil)\nحِكْمَةٌۢ بَالِغَةٌ‌ فَمَا تُغْنِ النُّذُرُۙ‏(5)\nHEKMATUN BAALEGHATUN FAMAA TUGHNE AN-NUZURU.\nConsummate wisdom, but (they) availed not (of) the warnings\nفَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ‌ۘ يَوْمَ يَدْعُ الدَّاعِ اِلٰى شَىْءٍ نُّكُرٍۙ‏(6)\nFA TAWALLA A’NHUM YAWMA YADU’U DAA-E’ ELAA SHAY-IN NNUKURIN.\nSo withdraw from them thyself (O Our Apostle Muhammad!) On the day when the Caller shall call them unto the hard task (of Reckoning)\nخُشَّعًا اَبْصَارُهُمْ يَخْرُجُوْنَ مِنَ الْاَجْدَاثِ كَاَنَّهُمْ جَرَادٌ مُّنْتَشِرٌۙ‏(7)\nKHUSSHAA’AN AABSAARUHUM YAKHROJOONA MENAL AJDAASE KA-ANNAHUM JARAADUN MMUNTASHERUN.\nWith their eyes cast down, they shall go forth from their graves as if they were locusts scattered\nمُّهْطِعِيْنَ اِلَى الدَّاعِ‌ؕ يَقُوْلُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ هٰذَا يَوْمٌ عَسِرٌ‏(8)\nMMUHTEE’EENA ELAL AD-DAAE’E YAQOOLO KAAFEROON HAAZAA YAWMUL A’ASERUN.\nHastening unto the Caller; Shall say the disbelievers: ‘This is a hard day!\nكَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوْحٍ فَكَذَّبُوْا عَبْدَنَا وَقَالُوْا مَجْنُوْنٌ وَّازْدُجِرَ‏(9)\nKAZZABAT QABLAHUM QAWMO NOOHIN FA KAZZABOO A’ABDANAA WA QAALOO MAJNOONUN WWAAZDUJERA.\nBelied before them the people of Noah (their apostles), so they belied Our servant and said they (he was) “Mad “ and he was driven out\nفَدَعَا رَبَّهٗۤ اَنِّىْ مَغْلُوْبٌ فَانْتَصِرْ‏(10)\nFA-DA-A’A WAL AANNEAA MAGHLOOBUN FAANTASER.\nSo he called upon his Lord (saying): ‘Verily, I am overcome (by these people), so give help\nفَفَتَحْنَاۤ اَبْوَابَ السَّمَآءِ بِمَآءٍ مُّنْهَمِرٍ ۖ‏(11)\nFAFATAHNAA ABWAABAS SAMAAA-E BEMAAA-IM MUNHAMER.\nSo opened We the gates of heaven with water pouring down\nوَّفَجَّرْنَا الْاَرْضَ عُيُوْنًا فَالْتَقَى الْمَآءُ عَلٰٓى اَمْرٍ قَدْ قُدِرَ‌ۚ‏(12)\nWA FAJJARNAL ARZA O’YOONAN FALTAQAL MAAA-O A’LAA AMRIN QAD QODER.\nAnd We caused the earth to break forth like springs and water from the heavens and the earth met together for the purpose verily destined\nوَحَمَلْنٰهُ عَلٰى ذَاتِ اَلْوَاحٍ وَّدُسُرٍۙ‏(13)\nWAHAMALNAAHU A’LAA ZAATIL AALWAAHIN WWADUSURIN.\nAnd We bore him on a thing made of planks and nails\nتَجْرِىْ بِاَعْيُنِنَا‌ۚ جَزَآءً لِّمَنْ كَانَ كُفِرَ‏(14)\nTAJREE BEAAA’YUNENAA JA-ZAAA-AWN LEMAN KAANA KUFERA.\nIt floated on, before Our eyes, a recompense for those who had been rejected (by the infidels)\nوَلَقَدْ تَّرَكْنٰهَاۤ اٰيَةً فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(15)\nWA LAQAD TTARAKNAAHAA AAYATAL FA HAL MIN MMUDDAKERIN.\nAnd indeed, We have left it (the Ark) as a sign, but is there one to remember (it)?\nفَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(16)\nFA-KAYFA KAANA A’AZAABEAA WANUZURE.\nHow (great) was then My chastisement and My warning!\nوَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا الْقُرْاٰنَ لِلذِّكْرِ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(17)\nWA LAQAD YASSARNAA QURAANA LELZZEKRE FA HAL MIN MMUDDAKERIN.\nAnd indeed, have We made Qur’an easy (for remembrance ), but is there one to remember (it)?\nكَذَّبَتْ عَادٌ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(18)\nKAZZABAT A’ADUN FA-KAYFA KAANA A’AZAABEAA WANUZURE.\nBelied (the truth) (the people of) ‘Ad, then how (great) was My chastisement and My warning!\nاِنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ رِيْحًا صَرْصَرًا فِىْ يَوْمِ نَحْسٍ مُّسْتَمِرٍّۙ‏(19)\nINNAA ARSALNAA A’LAYHIM REEHAN SARSARAN FEE YAWMIL NAHSIN MMUSTAMERRIN.\n(Lo!) Verily sent We on them a violent wind, on a Day of constant ill-luck\nتَنْزِعُ النَّاسَۙ كَاَنَّهُمْ اَعْجَازُ نَخْلٍ مُّنْقَعِرٍ‏(20)\nTANZEU’U NAASA KA-ANNAHUM AAA’JAAZU NAKHLIN MMUNQAE’ERIN.\nFlinging the people away, as if they were palm-trunks uprooted\nفَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(21)\nFA-KAYFA KAANA A’AZAABEAA WANUZURE.\nHow (great) was then My chastisement and My warning!\nوَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا الْقُرْاٰنَ لِلذِّكْرِ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(22)\nWA LAQAD YASSARNAA QURAANA LELZZEKRE FA HAL MIN MMUDDAKERIN.\nAnd indeed, have We made Qur’an easy (to remember), but is there one to remember (it)?\nكَذَّبَتْ ثَمُوْدُ بِالنُّذُرِ‏(23)\nKAZZABAT SAMOODO BEALNNUZURE.\n(The people of) Thamood belied the warners\nفَقَالُوْۤا اَبَشَرًا مِّنَّا وَاحِدًا نَّتَّبِعُهٗۤۙ اِنَّاۤ اِذًا لَّفِىْ ضَلٰلٍ وَّسُعُرٍ‏(24)\nFA-QAALOO AABASHARAN MINNAA WAAHEDAN NNATTABEU’UH INNAA EZAL LAFEE ZALAALIM WWASUU’URIN.\nAnd said they: ‘What! A single man, from among us! and we to follow him? Verily then we shall be astray and in distress\nءَاُلْقِىَ الذِّكْرُ عَلَيْهِ مِنْۢ بَيْنِنَا بَلْ هُوَ كَذَّابٌ اَشِرٌ‏(25)\nAALQEAAA AZ-ZEKRU A’LAYHE MIN BAYNENAA BAL HOWA KAZZAABUN AASHERUN.\nIs it that (the duty of) reminding hath been bestowed on him (alone), of all the (people) among us? Nay! He is a great liar, an insolent one!\nسَيَعْلَمُوْنَ غَدًا مَّنِ الْكَذَّابُ الْاَشِرُ‏(26)\nSA-YA’LAMOONA GHADAN MMANE AL-KAZZAABU AL-AASHERU.\nSoon they shall know on the morrow, (as to) who is the liar, the Insolent One!\nاِنَّا مُرْسِلُوا النَّاقَةِ فِتْنَةً لَّهُمْ فَارْتَقِبْهُمْ وَاصْطَبِرْ‏(27)\nINNAA MURSELOOA AN-NAAQATE FETNATAN LAHUM FAARTAQEBHUM WAASTABER.\n(O’ Our Apostle Saleh!) verily We are going to send the she- camel as a trial for them; so watch them and be patient\nوَنَبِّئْهُمْ اَنَّ الْمَآءَ قِسْمَةٌۢ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ۚ كُلُّ شِرْبٍ مُّحْتَضَرٌ‏(28)\nWANABBEHUM ANNAL MAAA-AH QESMATUN BAYNAHUM KULLO SHERBIN MMUHTAZARUN.\nAnd (thou O’ Saleh!) make them aware (beforehand) that the water is (to be) divided between them; and every drinking share shall be witnessed (on it)\nفَنَادَوْا صَاحِبَهُمْ فَتَعَاطٰى فَعَقَرَ‏(29)\nFANAADAWA SAAHEBAHUM FATAA’AATAA FAA’AQARA.\nBut they called their companion, then he pursued (her) and hamstrung (her)\nفَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(30)\nFA-KAYFA KAANA A’AZAABEAA WANUZURE.\nHow (great) was My chastisement and My warning?\nاِنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ صَيْحَةً وَّاحِدَةً فَكَانُوْا كَهَشِيْمِ الْمُحْتَظِرِ‏(31)\nINNAA ARSALNAA A’LAYHIM SAYHATANW WAAHEDATAN FA KAANOO KAHASHEEME AL-MUHTAZERE.\nVerily sent We upon them a single (violent) blast, and they were (all) like the dry stubble used by a fencer in a fence\nوَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا الْقُرْاٰنَ لِلذِّكْرِ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(32)\nWA LAQAD YASSARNAA QURAANA LELZZEKRE FA HAL MIN MMUDDAKERIN.\nAnd indeed, have We made Qur’an easy (to remember) but is there any rememberer?\nكَذَّبَتْ قَوْمُ لُوْطٍ ۢ بِالنُّذُرِ‏(33)\nKAZZABAT QAWMO LOOTIM BEALNNUZURE.\nThe people of Lot belied the warners\nاِنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ حَاصِبًا اِلَّاۤ اٰلَ لُوْطٍ‌ؕ نَّجَّيْنٰهُمْ بِسَحَرٍۙ‏(34)\nINNAA ARSALNAA A’LAYHIM HAASEBAN ILLAA AALA LOOTIN NNAJJAYNAAHUM BESAHARIN.\nVerily sent We upon them a stone-storm, (which destroyed them all) save the followers of Lot; We saved them by early dawn\nنِّعْمَةً مِّنْ عِنْدِنَا‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِىْ مَنْ شَكَرَ‏(35)\nNNEA’MATAN MIN I’NDENAA KAZAALEKA NAJZEAA MAN SHAKARA.\n(As) a bounty from unto Us; Thus do We recompense him who giveth thanks\nوَلَقَدْ اَنْذَرَهُمْ بَطْشَتَنَا فَتَمَارَوْا بِالنُّذُرِ‏(36)\nWA LAQAD AANZARAHUM BATSHATANAA FATAMAARAWA BEALNNUZURE.\nAnd indeed, he did warn them of Our severe seizure, but they did dispute about the warner\nوَلَقَدْ رَاوَدُوْهُ عَنْ ضَيْفِهٖ فَطَمَسْنَاۤ اَعْيُنَهُمْ فَذُوْقُوْا عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(37)\nWA LAQAD RAAWADOOHU A’N ZAYFEH FATAMASNAA AAA’YUNAHUM FA-ZOOQOO A’AZAABEAA WANUZURE.\nAnd indeed, they did demand him of his guests (for their evil desert), so did We blind their eyes (saying)’. ‘Taste ye then My chastisement and My warning!\nوَلَقَدْ صَبَّحَهُمْ بُكْرَةً عَذَابٌ مُّسْتَقِرٌّ‌ ۚ‏(38)\nWA LAQAD SABBAHAHUM BUKRATANW A’ZAABUN MMUSTAQERRUN.\nAnd indeed, dawned on them in the morn a lasting chastisement\nفَذُوْقُوْا عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(39)\nFA-ZOOQOO A’AZAABEAA WANUZURE.\nNow taste ye My chastisement and My warning!\nوَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا الْقُرْاٰنَ لِلذِّكْرِ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(40)\nWA LAQAD YASSARNAA QURAANA LELZZEKRE FA HAL MIN MMUDDAKERIN.\nAnd indeed, have We made Qur’an easy (to he remembered) but is there any one to remember (it)?\nوَلَقَدْ جَآءَ اٰلَ فِرْعَوْنَ النُّذُرُ‌ۚ‏(41)\nWA LAQAD JAAA-A AALA FIR-A’WNA AN-NUZURU.\nAnd indeed, came unto the people of Pharaoh the warners\nكَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا كُلِّهَا فَاَخَذْنٰهُمْ اَخْذَ عَزِيْزٍ مُّقْتَدِرٍ‏(42)\nKAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA KULLEHAA FAAKHAZNAAHUM AAKHZA A’AZEEZIN MMUQTADERIN.\nThey belied all Our signs so did We seize them after the manner of the one the Ever Prevalent, the All-Mighty One\nاَكُفَّارُكُمْ خَيْرٌ مِّنْ اُولٰٓئِكُمْ اَمْ لَكُمْ بَرَآءَةٌ فِى الزُّبُرِ‌ۚ‏(43)\nAAKUFFAARUKUM KHAYRUL MIN AOOLAAAEKUM AM LAKUM BARAAATUN FIL AZ-ZUBURE.\nWhat! Are your disbelievers (O’ ye Meccans!) better people than these? Or is there an exemption for you in the sacred Scriptures?\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ نَحْنُ جَمِيْعٌ مُّنْتَصِرٌ‏(44)\nAM YAQOOLOONA NAHNO JAMEE-U’L MMUNTASERUN.\nOr say they: “We are a host joined together to help each other?\nسَيُهْزَمُ الْجَمْعُ وَيُوَلُّوْنَ الدُّبُرَ‏(45)\nSAYUHZAMU AL-JAMU’U WA YOWALLOONAL AD-DUBURA.\nSoon shall the host be routed, and they shall turn their backs\nبَلِ السَّاعَةُ مَوْعِدُهُمْ وَالسَّاعَةُ اَدْهٰى وَاَمَرُّ‏(46)\nBALIL SAA-A’TO MAWE’EDUHUM WA SAA-A’TO AADHAA WAAMARRU.\nNay! The Hour (of Reckoning) is their promised time, and the Hour shall be most grievous and bitter\nاِنَّ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ وَّسُعُرٍ‌ۘ‏(47)\nINNAL MUJREMEEN FEE ZALAALIM WWASUU’URIN.\nVerily the guilty ones are straying and mad (in distress)\nيَوْمَ يُسْحَبُوْنَ فِى النَّارِ عَلٰى وُجُوْهِهِمْؕ ذُوْقُوْا مَسَّ سَقَرَ‏(48)\nYAWMA YUSHABOONA FIL NAAR A’LAA WUJOOHEHEM ZOOQOO MASSAN SAQARA.\nOn that Day they shall be dragged upon their faces into the fire (and it will be said unto them)’. ‘Taste ye (now) the touch of Hell!\nاِنَّا كُلَّ شَىْءٍ خَلَقْنٰهُ بِقَدَرٍ‏(49)\nINNAA KULLA SHAY-IN KHALAQNAAHO BEQADARIN.\nVerily every thing have We created to a determined measure\nوَمَاۤ اَمْرُنَاۤ اِلَّا وَاحِدَةٌ كَلَمْحٍۢ بِالْبَصَرِ‏(50)\nWA MAA AAMRUNAA ILLAA WAAHEDATUN KALAMHIN BIL-BASARE.\nAnd Our command is but one (word ‘Be’! And it becometh) like the twinkling of an eye\nوَلَقَدْ اَهْلَكْنَاۤ اَشْيَاعَكُمْ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(51)\nWA LAQAD AHLAKNAL AASHYAAA’AKUM FA HAL MIN MMUDDAKERIN.\nAnd indeed, have We destroyed the like unto you, but is there any one to receive the warning?\nوَكُلُّ شَىْءٍ فَعَلُوْهُ فِى الزُّبُرِ‏(52)\nWA KULLO SHAY-IN FAA’ALOOHU FIL AZ-ZUBURE.\nAnd everything they have done is in the books (of deeds)\nوَ كُلُّ صَغِيْرٍ وَّكَبِيْرٍ مُّسْتَطَرٌ‏(53)\nWA KULLO SAGHEERIN WWAKABEERIN MMUSTATARUN.\nEvery matter small and big, is (correctly) recorded in writing\nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّنَهَرٍۙ‏(54)\nINNAL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN FEE JANNAATIN WWANAHARIN.\nVerily, the pious ones shall be in gardens and rivers\nفِىْ مَقْعَدِ صِدْقٍ عِنْدَ مَلِيْكٍ مُّقْتَدِرٍ‏(55)\nFEE MAQA’ADE SEDQIN I’NDAL MALEEKIN MMUQTADERIN.\nIn the seat of Truth, with the Sovereign Omnipotent One",
  "merits": "Surah al-Qamar (The Moon)\nThis ’Makki’ Surah has 55 verses. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the fact of the person who recites this Surah will shine like the full moon on the Day of Reckoning. The best time to recite this Surah is at night and this carries the highest reward.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that the one who recites this Surah will have a mount from Jannah on which he will sit when he wakes from his grave. Whoever keeps this Surah under his cap or turban at the time of Friday prayers will be highly respected by the people and his difficulties will be eased."
}
